  "title": "fix round 1 for T-1370: test harness drops live claude executor rows; shipped-row test reads the repo pool.toml directly",
  "spec": "Fix round for T-1370 (held gate_red, worktree wt/T-1370, commit adds the claude:opus row + [models].opus = claude-opus-5-5). Cause: tests/_harness.py copies the repo .orchestrator/pool.toml into the per-process TMP root (tests/_harness.py:11-20), and 12 existing tests (test_pool.Executors.*, test_executor.Executor.*, test_daemon.Daemon.test_free_slots_*, test_daemon.Daemon.test_fallback_skips_complexity_without_tier, test_cli.Cli.test_status_plain_and_json) assume the live executor set is Codex rows only. The harness already neutralises operator settings the same way (planner autonomous forced false, B's planner affinity removed).\nFix, keeping the pool.toml change exactly as committed:\n1. tests/_harness.py: when copying pool.toml, drop every [[executors]] section whose body has provider = \"claude\" (same section-split loop already there), with a comment: live routed Claude rows are an operator setting; tests that need one build it.\n2. tests/test_pool.py::test_shipped_pool_toml_claude_opus_row_is_valid: load REPO/.orchestrator/pool.toml (REPO from _harness) with tomllib and build Pool(cfg=that dict); assert the claude:opus executor exists, provider \"claude\", enabled True, model == cfg[\"models\"][\"opus\"] == \"claude-opus-5-5\". It must not depend on the TMP copy. If Pool(cfg) touches state files, it uses the harness TMP root as other Pool(cfg) tests do.\nDo not edit any other test or production code; the 12 failing tests must pass unchanged.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_pool.py::test_shipped_pool_toml_claude_opus_row_is_valid",
    "tests/test_pool.py::test_bands_and_enabled",
    "tests/test_executor.py::test_start_routes_through_pick_executor",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_free_slots_uses_claude_capacity_under_fallback",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/<this task> exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "tests/_harness.py",
    "tests/test_pool.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
