  "result": {
    "summary": "The failures come from the shared test harness inheriting the newly enabled Claude executor. Existing tests assume a Codex-only pool.\n\nMay I add `tests/_harness.py` to the write scope? The proposed fix excludes Claude executor rows from the harness\u2019s temporary fixture; the shipped-config acceptance test still reads the real TOML and verifies Opus is enabled.\n\nThe original packet explicitly permits edits only to `.orchestrator/pool.toml` and `tests/test_pool.py`, so this requires a scope extension. Current commit remains `01552aea385823f797ad308e3f2b5c58912883f2`; the worktree is clean and the gate remains red.",
